# keypad_attempts.dialogue — reactions when a portrait date is tried on the lab keypad.
# played over the open keypad by ui/keypad_panel.gd, the first time each date is entered.
# the panel sets keypad_companion_present just before (true when Layla is following).

~ greene_birthday
if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_companion_present") == true:
	Layla: So it isn't his birthdate...
	Player: Seems like it.
	Player: Well, I suppose it would've been too easy if it were that.
	Layla: Let's look around more.
	Player: Yep.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
=> after_portrait_date

~ ember_birthday
if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_companion_present") == true:
	if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_tried_greene_birthday") == true:
		Player: Well, so it isn't Dr. Ember's birthdate either.
	else
		Player: Well, so it isn't Dr. Ember's birthdate.
	Layla: Right. That one was a long shot anyway.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
		Player: Yeah, I don't think there's anything like that between them.
		Layla: You think so?
		Layla: I think Dr. Ember might have a thing for him...
		Player: Even though she's always at his throat?
		Layla: Yeah! That's precisely why I think so!
		Layla: They'll be like a classic enemies-to-lovers trope!
		Layla: And it'll be glorious.
		Player: Hmm.
		Player: Interesting.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
=> after_portrait_date

~ after_portrait_date
if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_tried_greene_birthday") == true and Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_tried_ember_birthday") == true:
	=> both_portraits_tried
=> END

~ both_portraits_tried
if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_companion_present") == true:
	Player: So, we've tried both the dates from the portraits in here.
	Player: Looks like we need to try something else.
	if Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked") == true and Flags.get_level_flag("dna_dates_found") == false:
		Layla: We should probably look into that date thing Julian mentioned.
		Player: Right, that's a better lead.
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_pointed_to_biochem") == true:
		Layla: We should probably look around the building for more clues.
		Player: Right, there's gotta be something more substantial here.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
=> END

~ voss_birthday
if Flags.get_level_flag("keypad_companion_present") == true:
	Layla: Oh. So it wasn't Leon Voss's birthday.
	Player: Seems like it.
	Player: (I'm glad it isn't.)
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
=> END

~ miescher_discovery
# step 2.269: the nuclein letter date failed on the lab keypad. staged in its own overlay
# (miescher_keypad_advanced_overlay.tscn; the keypad closes first). every version unlocks 4F.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
# step 2.376: Layla's expressions (rig). she enters as "base"; this lands while she fades in. she's just
# watched the code fail.
do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
if Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked") == true and (Flags.get_level_flag("miescher_book_date_seen") == true or Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged") == true):
	=> miescher_natural
# step 2.288: the date tried without the book page or the phone, or before julian's lead. fiona
# decides on the office herself, then the scene joins layla's reaction to that idea.
do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
Player: You know, I don't know why...
Player: But having this code fail makes me feel like we probably won't find the code here.
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: We should probably look in his office. Cut to the chase.
=> miescher_office_idea

~ miescher_natural
# the date came from the book page and/or layla's phone, after julian's lead.
do actor_change("Fiona", "suspicious")
Player: Huh. Seems like this... isn't it.
if Flags.get_level_flag("miescher_book_date_seen") == true and Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged") == true:
	Player: That's weird. The book and the internet both pointed toward this date.
elif Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged") == true:
	do actor_change("Layla", "whining")
	Layla: No! But that... can't be. We literally looked it up!
else
	do actor_change("Fiona", "sad")
	Player: I was so certain it would be this. I verified it through the book in the library.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: So, what now?
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "whining")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: Oh no! What are we gonna do now?
do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged") == true:
	Layla: Should I just... send an email to the professor? Requesting extra days?
else
	Layla: Should I email the professor once my phone's alive?
do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
Player: ...
# she looks up (same pose)
do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: No. We have another way.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: Sure. Like what?
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
	Layla: Really? What would that be, Fiona?
	do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: We look for clues in his office?
~ miescher_office_idea
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "angry_talk")
	Layla: Listen, that's probably illegal.
	Layla: Surely you must know that?
	do actor_change("Layla", "angry")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "wowed")
	Layla: His... OFFICE?
	# the comic shock (her funny set), then a fists-pout while Fiona talks her round
	do actor_change("Layla", "funny_shock")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "shock")
	Layla: Nooooooo! That sounds so...
	Layla: ILLEGAL.
	do actor_change("Layla", "huffy")
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: Maybe. But... if I remember correctly, there aren't any cameras on the faculty office floor.
Player: And, there's barely anyone in this building anyway.
Player: And, if I'm being really honest...
do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
Player: I'm kinda having fun trying to break in.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "suspicious")
	Layla stares at you, unconvinced.
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: Fine.
	Layla: Just... don't drag me into it.
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
	Layla looks at you like a confused puppy trying to figure out what its human wants it to do.
	do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
	Layla: Ummm... okay, Fiona.
	do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
	Layla: I just... don't want you to get into trouble for me.
	do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
do actor_change("Fiona", "shrug")
Player: Fair. But honestly, there's no way they'll do anything to me.
Player: The lab is way too dependent on me.
Player: And even if the professor does find out, I'm sure I'll be able to wiggle my way out of it, somehow.
do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
Layla: You sound... like you're rather experienced in this regard.
do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
Player: Sometimes a girl's gotta do what she's gotta do, you know?
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Let's go?
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: Fine. Let's go.
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
	Layla: Let's go!
do Flags.set_level_flag("faculty_floor_unlocked", true)
do show_hint_banner("Floor 4F (Faculty Offices) is now accessible.")
=> END

# step 2.286: dates from threads of inheritance, either format. the day-first (_dm) versions add the
